# VCP behavioral test pyramid (mandatory)

Agents MUST deliver this pyramid **by default** for every significant
behavioral change. Do **not** wait for the user to ask for invariants /
proptest / battle / E2E / a smoke runbook. Skipping layers is a process
failure unless the change is explicitly cosmetic (see exceptions).

Full detail, ASCII diagram, and command placeholders live in the
`quality-assurance` skill §1. Stack: Topcoat (Rust full-stack) — see
the `web-stack` skill.

## Layers (every behavioral surface)

| Layer | Role | Typical artifact |
|-------|------|------------------|
| **Unit** | Local happy / sad paths | `#[test]` / `#[tokio::test]` in module |
| **Invariants** | Source shape is the contract | `include_str` / grep pins / `check_*.sh` |
| **Proptest** | Property over a space of inputs | `proptest!` / table of random corpora |
| **Battle** | Contention / multi-thread / flood | `battle_*` with `Barrier` / parallel load |
| **E2E** | Real product seam already in tree | `*_e2e_test.rs`, page+DB+session path |
| **Smoke runbook** | Staging ops checklist CI cannot replace | `docs/runbooks/*_smoke_test.md` |

One-liner mnemonic:

> unit = *what*, invariants = *how the code must look*, proptest = *for
> all*, battle = *under contention*, E2E = *in the system*, runbook =
> *on staging*.

```
                    ╱╲
                   ╱  ╲     Smoke runbook (staging ops)
                  ╱────╲
                 ╱      ╲   E2E (product seams)
                ╱────────╲
               ╱          ╲ Battle (contention)
              ╱────────────╲
             ╱              ╲ Proptest (properties)
            ╱────────────────╲
           ╱                  ╲ Invariants (source pins)
          ╱────────────────────╲
         ╱                      ╲ Unit (local behavior)
        ╱────────────────────────╲
```

Postgres for DB-backed layers: `vcp_test` via `just db-create-test`
(`config/testing.toml`).
## When the full pyramid is REQUIRED

Treat as behavioral (full pyramid) any change that alters:

- Auth / session / CSRF / login-logout lifecycle
- Casbin / `PermissionContext` / role or policy files
- Tenant / organization membership and isolation (IDOR surfaces)
- License, entitlement, download, or billing / webhook paths
- Cookie / timezone localization that affects legal or billing display
- New Topcoat pages, layouts, shards, or procedures on those seams
- Rate limiting, audit events, or secret handling

Even a “small” refactor on these seams needs the pyramid.

## Exceptions (pyramid may be thinned)

Only these may skip proptest / battle / E2E / new runbook:

- Comment-only or non-executable doc typos
- Pure formatting (`cargo fmt` / `topcoat fmt`) with no semantic diff
- Pure literal readability renames with identical semantics
  (e.g. `Duration::from_secs(3600)` → `Duration::from_hours(1)`)
  — still keep a trivial unit equality assert when touching a const

When in doubt, deliver the **full** pyramid.

## Planning and definition of done

- Plans and implementation todos MUST list pyramid deliverables per
  surface (not a vague “add tests”).
- A task is **not done** after clippy + a few unit tests alone.
- Prefer extending an existing `*_e2e_test.rs` / pin suite / runbook
  over inventing a parallel harness.
- Denial paths are mandatory on auth / tenancy / entitlement changes
  (wrong org, expired session, missing permission, missing entitlement).
- New smoke runbooks: audience, severity, automated prerequisites,
  Pass / Fail criteria, related links. Link from the nearest operator
  doc when one exists.

## Forbidden agent behavior

| Forbidden | Required instead |
|-----------|------------------|
| “Cosmetic refactor, unit tests enough” on auth/tenant/billing | Full pyramid |
| Plan that omits invariants / proptest / battle / E2E / runbook | Explicit per-layer todos |
| Stop after clippy + one happy-path unit test | Execute filters covering every new layer |
| Invent a second auth/tenant path “just for tests” | Exercise the production seam |
| Copy bastion IPC / proxy / recording test harnesses blindly | Portal-appropriate seams only |

Use the host toolchain as installed; do not force `rustup run` /
toolchain overrides unless the user asks.
